 exercising executive power within France. It emerged during the tumultuous period of the French Revolution, a time marked by radical societal change and the quest for liberty, equality, and fraternity. Key figures such as Maximilien Robespierre and Georges Danton played instrumental roles in shaping this government, which sought to break away from the monarchical traditions of the Ancien Régime, emphasizing the importance of civic rights and popular sovereignty.

